      "title": "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a Linear System With Variables Other Than x, y, z"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ac9403e1-a0b4-57a0-858b-157a7f07ef09",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+3q &=8 \\\\ 5p+7q &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order $p,q$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient.\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
